  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Local Systems in Agriculture (ELSA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  ELSA addresses a range of agriculture sector development challenges, including lack of access to inputs needed for agriculture production, and weak local systems that negatively impact those who produce, distribute, sell, and consume agricultural products. ELSA was launched on October 1, 2024, and will work primarily with local partners, including farmers and the myriad businesses involved in the agriculture value chain between farmers and final consumers.  Through ELSA, USAID will not only create and strengthen these points of connection, but also facilitate &quot;value addition&quot; or product improvements, at each stage along the way. ELSA will also further the Agency&apos;s localization priorities by building the capacity of local partners in areas such as internal policies and procedures, financial and compliance management, proposal writing, and risk-mitigation strategies.  Capacity building under ELSA will equip local partners with needed internal systems enabling them to apply for direct USAID and/or other sources of funding after the activity ends.</narrative>
  </description>
